so this is the only record of what we started from. Do not change it except via
a superseding ADR.

The Excalidraw copyright notice and MIT permission notice must be retained in
all copies or substantial portions of the Software, and the notice in `LICENSE`
must not be removed or altered.

## Where Excalidraw code now lives

Phase 0 renamed package scopes and moved the app directory. Upstream paths are
given so the origin stays traceable.

| Area | Upstream path | Path in this repository |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Geometry primitives | `packages/math/` | `packages/math/` (unrenamed) |
| Constants, colours, utility types, event bus | `packages/common/` | `packages/common/` |
| Element schema, scene container | `packages/element/` | `packages/element/` |
| Hit testing | `packages/element/src/collision.ts` | same |
| Hand-drawn shape generation (roughjs) | `packages/element/src/shape.ts` | same |
| Element canvas rendering, bitmap caches | `packages/element/src/renderElement.ts` | same |
| Editor library (component, actions, renderer) | `packages/excalidraw/` | `packages/editor/` |
| File-format migrations | `packages/excalidraw/data/restore.ts` | `packages/editor/data/restore.ts` |
| Toolbar, panel, colour picker, dialogs | `packages/excalidraw/components/` | `packages/editor/components/` |
| Host application | `excalidraw-app/` | `apps/web/` |
| Fractional indexing (z-order) | `packages/fractional-indexing/` | same (CC0-1.0, see below) |

`packages/math/` deliberately keeps its upstream directory name in Phase 0. The
architecture documents describe it as `packages/geometry/`, which is where it
lands when the package is curated in Phase 1 — renaming it now would only add
churn to a phase whose job is to produce a working build.

Internal `Excalidraw*` type and symbol names are also still upstream's. They are
renamed in Phase 3, deliberately deferred so that the Phase 1 and 2 diffs stay
reviewable against upstream.

