## @firo/fractional-indexing — CC0-1.0

The fractional-indexing package vendored from Excalidraw is licensed **CC0-1.0**
(public domain dedication), *not* MIT. This is a deliberate upstream choice and
is compatible with our MIT licence. If you replace it, preserve the CC0 notice
or replace it with an equivalently permissive implementation.

```
CC0 1.0 Universal — https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Derived from rocicorp/fractional-indexing
```

## Fonts — see FONT-LICENSES.md

**Virgil and Excalifont were removed in Phase 0 and are not shipped.** Virgil
is a commercial font with no redistribution grant anywhere in the upstream
repository; Excalifont is a modified Virgil and inherits the same problem. Virgil
was also the *default* font, so removing it changed the product's default
typeface.

```
Virgil     — Four Black Studios. Commercial. No licence file upstream. NOT SHIPPED.
Excalifont — Ján Filípek / DizajnDesign, derived from Virgil. NOT SHIPPED.
```

**The remaining bundled fonts are not yet cleared.** The repository contains no
licence file for any font. See [`FONT-LICENSES.md`](FONT-LICENSES.md) for the
per-font audit, which is a **release blocker**: the default face (Nunito) is
believed to be SIL OFL 1.1 but that is unverified, and no OFL text is shipped
alongside the binaries.

`AGENTS.md` forbids shipping an unlicensed font file. Adding a font without
adding its licence text in the same commit violates it.

